<sheets><sheet><plain><text x="20" y="412" size="3.4" layer="97" ratio="8">Isolated Line Test Set - a lineman's handset, polarity independent, line powered</text>
<text x="20" y="400" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">leads -&gt; F1 100mA -&gt; R1/R2 100R -&gt; RV1 + C1 snubber -&gt; BR1 bridge -&gt; K1 hook -&gt; T1 wet 600:600 -&gt; hybrid</text>
<text x="20" y="392" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">TALK: 600R termination, off-hook, earpiece and electret.  MONITOR: 10k bridge, no load, volume to earpiece.</text>
<text x="20" y="380" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">DC loop in TALK: R1 100 + R2 100 + K1 + T1 primary 40-150 = 240-350 R, under the 400 R limit.</text>
<text x="20" y="368" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">The bridge rectifier is why the leads can go on either way round - the rest of the circuit always sees one polarity.</text>
<text x="20" y="356" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">Line powered: the electret bias (R7) and the line-present LED (R8) come from the rectified loop. No battery.</text>
<text x="20" y="344" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">SAFETY: T1 must be the wet type. A dry voice transformer saturates on 20-50 mA of loop current.</text>
<text x="20" y="332" size="2.2" layer="97" ratio="8">Isolation line to touchable metal must hold 5 Mohm at 100 V DC. Measure after assembly.</text>
<frame x1="0" y1="0" x2="520" y2="420" columns="8" rows="6" layer="91" border-left="yes" border-top="yes" border-right="yes" border-bottom="yes"/>
